   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "-er verbs",
     "texto": [
      "Most French verbs end in **-er**. The regular ones, such as **parler** (to speak), **habiter** (to live) and **travailler** (to work), follow the same pattern; **aller** (to go) is a common irregular exception.",
      "With regular verbs, you drop **-er** and add the endings: **-e, -es, -e, -ons, -ez, -ent**.",
      "What matters when speaking: **je parle, tu parles, il parle** and **ils parlent** sound **exactly the same** («parl»). The only ones that sound different are **nous parlons** and **vous parlez**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
